Slide 2: Introduction & Overview

What is Virtual Try-On?
• Advanced AI technology that enables customers to visualize clothing on themselves or models
• Addresses key challenges in online fashion retail:
  - High return rates (20-40% average)
  - Purchase uncertainty
  - Lack of personalized experiences

Our Solution:
• High-resolution (768×1024) virtual try-on
• AI-powered recommendations
• Real-time AR capabilities
• Inclusive design for diverse demographics

---

Slide 3: Core Technology & Architecture

VITON-HD Architecture
Three-Stage Deep Learning Pipeline:

1. Segmentation Generator (U-Net)
   - Parses body parts from agnostic representation
   - Outputs 13-channel semantic segmentation map

2. Geometric Matching Module (GMM)
   - Warps clothing using Thin-Plate Spline transformation
   - Aligns garments with person's pose and body shape

3. ALIAS Generator
   - Synthesizes final try-on result
   - Uses Adaptive Layer-Instance normalization
   - Produces photo-realistic outputs

